<hr class=3D"c5" width=3D"20%" noshade=3D"">
<div class=3D"c4"><a class=3D"c6" name=3D"genre" id=3D"genre">Genders</a></=
div>
<p>The Universal Language has three genders:<br>
Masculine, Feminine and Neuter.</p>
<p>One may distinguish between them very easily.<br>
All <i>male</i> beings are of the <i>masculine</i> gender;<br>
All <i>female</i> beings are of the <i>feminine</i> gender;<br>
All material objects and abstractions, as well as beings whose sex is unkno=
wn, are of the <i>neuter</i> gender.</p>
<p>The words always remain invariable; they never undergo any change.<br>
The feminine alone is indicated, in speech, by accenting the last vowel. On=
e marks the feminine in writing by placing a small horizontal line ( =C2=AF=
 ) over the final syllable. [Written here <i>after</i> the letter.]</p>
