<td><i>Ton</i> (your), <b>rm</b>;</td>
<td><i>Le poste</i> (police station), <b>sslf</b>;</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><i>Ton</i> (tone), <b>somfso</b>;</td>
<td><i>La bi=C3=A8re</i> (beer), <b>dsfr</b>;</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><i>La poste</i> (mail), <b>frl</b>;</td>
<td><i>La bi=C3=A8re</i> (bier), <b>sosdd</b>;</td>
</tr>
</tbody></table>
<table>
<tbody><tr>
<td></td>
<td>etc., etc.</td>
</tr>
</tbody></table>
<hr class=3D"c5" width=3D"20%" noshade=3D"">
<div class=3D"c4"><a class=3D"c6" name=3D"vbs" id=3D"vbs">Verbs</a></div>
<p><b>Solresol</b> verbs always have the same form (present infinitive).</p=
>
<table>
<caption>EXAMPLE:</caption>
<tbody><tr>
<td><i>begin</i>, <b>sdf</b>;</td>
<td><i>I begin,</i> <b>dr sdf</b></td>
</tr>
</tbody></table>
<p>To mark tenses and moods, one employs <b>dd, rr, mm, ff, soso, ll, ss</b=
>.</p>
<p>To abbreviate these forms in writing, one uses capital <b>D</b> in the p=
lace of <b>dd</b>, capital <b>R</b> for <b>rr</b>, <b>M</b> for <b>mm</b>, =
<b>F</b> for <b>ff</b>, <b>SO</b> for <b>soso</b>, <b>L</b> for <b>ll</b>, =
and <b>S</b> for <b>ss</b>.</p>
<div class=3D"c10"><b>D.</b> indicates</div>
<br>
1=C2=BA The imperfect indicative: <i>I begin,</i> <b>dr D sdf</b>, etc.<br>
2=C2=BA The pluperfect indicative: <i>I had begun</i>, <b>dr D sdf</b>, etc=
.
<div class=3D"c10"><b>R.</b> indicates</div>
<br>
1=C2=BA The simple past: <i>I began,</i> <b>dr R sdf</b>, etc.<br>
2=C2=BA The anterior past: <i>[as soon as/when] I had begun,</i> <b>dr R sd=
f</b>, etc.<br>
3=C2=BA The imperfect subjunctive: <i>that I might/should begin,</i> <b>mr =
dr R sdf</b>, etc.<br>
4=C2=BA The pluperfect subjunctive: <i>that I might/should have begun,</i> =
<b>mr dr, R sdf</b>.
<div class=3D"c10"><b>M.</b> marks</div>
<br>
1=C2=BA The future: <i>I will begin,</i> <b>dr M sdf</b>, etc., etc.<br>
2=C2=BA The future perfect: <i>I will have begun,</i> <b>dr M sdf</b>, etc.
<div class=3D"c10"><b>F.</b> marks</div>
<br>
1=C2=BA The present conditional: <i>I would begin,</i> <b>dr F sdf</b>, etc=
.<br>
2=C2=BA The perfect conditional: <i>I would have begun,</i> <b>dr F sdf</b>=
, etc.
<div class=3D"c10"><b>SO.</b> marks</div>
<br>
The imperative: <i>Let's begin</i>, <b>SO sdf</b>.
<div class=3D"c10"><b>L.</b> indicates</div>
<br>
1=C2=BA The present participle: <i>beginning,</i> <b>L sdf</b>.<br>
2=C2=BA The past (perfect) participle: <i>having begun,</i> <b>L sdf</b>.
<div class=3D"c10"><b>S.</b> marks</div>
<br>
The passive participle: <i>begun,</i> <b>S sdf</b>.
<hr class=3D"c5" width=3D"20%" noshade=3D"">
<div class=3D"c4"><a class=3D"c6" name=3D"subj" id=3D"subj">Subjunctive</a>=
</div>
<p>The subjunctive mood is marked by placing the word <b>mr</b>, <i>that</i=
>, before the personal pronouns.</p>
<div class=3D"c4">EXAMPLES:</div>
<blockquote><i>That I should commence,</i> <b>mr dr sdf.</b><br>
<i>That you should finish,</i> <b>mr dm fds.</b><br>
<i>May he/it progress,</i> <b>mr df sdl.</b><br>
<i>May she learn,</i> <b>mr df=C2=AF sds.</b><br>
<i>That we should study,</i> <b>mr dr' sdso.</b><br>
<i>That you [pl] should accomplish,</i> <b>mr dm' dsf.</b><br>
<i>That they [not f] should work,</i> <b>mr df' rsosr.</b><br>
<i>That they [f] should come,</i> <b>mr df'=C2=AF msod.</b><br>
<i>That you might write,</i> <b>mr dm R lmr.</b></blockquote>
<hr class=3D"c5" width=3D"20%" noshade=3D"">
<p class=3D"c7">We repeat this recommendation:<br>
In speech, it is necessary to pause slightly after every word in SOLRESOL, =
so that the listener may distinguish the words.</p>
<hr class=3D"c5" width=3D"20%" noshade=3D"">
<div class=3D"c4"><a class=3D"c6" name=3D"vpass" id=3D"vpass">Passive Verbs=
</a></div>
<p>We have just seen that the perfect tenses are conjugated without the aid=
 of any auxiliary verb. Only in the <i>passive verbs</i> do we use the auxi=
liary verb <i>Be,</i> <b>frm</b>.</p>
<div class=3D"c4">MODELS:</div>
<blockquote><i>To be loved,</i> <b>frm mls.</b><br>
<i>To have been loved,</i> <b>frm mls.</b><br>
<i>I am loved,</i> <b>dr frm mls.</b><br>
<i>I have been loved,</i> <b>dr frm mls</b>.<br>
<i>I was [being] detested,</i> <b>dr D frm slm.</b><br>
<i>I had been [being] detested,</i> <b>dr D frm slm</b>.<br>
<i>I was detested,</i> <b>dr R frm slm</b>.<br>
<i>I had been detested,</i> <b>dr R frm slm</b>.</blockquote>
<blockquote><i>I will be understood,</i> <b>dr M frm flf</b>.<br>
<i>I shall have been understood,</i> <b>dr M frm flf</b>.<br>
<i>I would be understood,</i> <b>dr F frm flf.</b><br>
<i>I would have been understood,</i> <b>dr F frm flf</b>.</blockquote>
<blockquote><i>Be accepted,</i> <b>frm dldm.</b><br>
<i>Let's be accepted,</i> <b>SO frm dldm.</b></blockquote>
<blockquote><i>That I should be refused,</i> <b>mr dr frm mdld.</b><br>
<i>That I should have received,</i> <b>mr dr frm msorso.</b></blockquote>
<blockquote><i>That I might be understood,</i> <b>mr dr R frm flf.</b><br>
<i>That I might have been understood,</i> <b>mr dr R frm flf.</b><br>
<i>Being understood,</i> <b>L frm flf.</b><br>
<i>Having been understood,</i> <b>L frm flf</b>.<br>
<i>Understood,</i> <b>S frm flf.</b></blockquote>
<hr class=3D"c5" width=3D"20%">
<div class=3D"c4"><a class=3D"c6" name=3D"vpron" id=3D"vpron">Reflexive Ver=
bs</a></div>
<p>One conjugates reflexive verbs by placing the second pronoun, that is, t=
he pronoun complement, after the verb.</p>
<div class=3D"c4">EXAMPLES:</div>
<blockquote><i>I amuse myself</i>, <b>dr lsr dr</b>.<br>
<i>You amuse yourself</i>, <b>dm lsr dm.</b><br>
<i>He amuses himself</i>, <b>df lsr dso.</b><br>
<i>She amuses herself</i>, <b>df=C2=AF lsr dso.</b></blockquote>
<hr class=3D"c5" width=3D"20%">
<div class=3D"c4"><a class=3D"c6" name=3D"vimp" id=3D"vimp">Impersonal Verb=
s</a></div>
<p>Here is the model for all impersonal verbs:</p>
