<hr class=3D"c5" width=3D"20%">
<div class=3D"c4"><a class=3D"c6" name=3D"inter" id=3D"inter">[Interrogatio=
n and Negation]</a></div>
<p>To use a verb interrogatively, simply put the personal pronoun after the=
 verb.</p>
<table>
<caption>EXAMPLES:</caption>
<tbody><tr>
<td><i>Am I?</i> <b>frm-dr?</b></td>
<td><i>Do we study?</i> <b>sdso-dr?</b></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><i>Do you want [to/that]?</i> <b>fsf-dm?</b></td>
<td><i>Are you learning?</i> <b>sds-dm?</b></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><i>Does he understand?</i> <b>flf-df?</b></td>
<td><i>Do they love?</i> <b>mls-df'?</b></td>
</tr>
</tbody></table>
<p>Negation is indicated by placing <b>d</b> before the word to be negated.=
</p>
<div class=3D"c4">EXAMPLES:</div>
<blockquote><i>I do not love,</i> <b>dr d mls.</b><br>
<i>Don't you want [to/that]?</i> <b>d fsf-dm?</b><br>
<i>Won't it rain?</i> <b>d M ssd so?</b><br>
<i>Why don't we continue this study?</i> <b>fso d F rsoml-dr' fm sd?</b><br=
>
<i>Let's not go there,</i> <b>d So frf lm,</b>.<br>
<i>It is necessary never to act unwisely in order not to be sick,</i> <b>Ls=
o fld fsol dsfd md d ffdr.</b></blockquote>
<hr class=3D"c5" width=3D"70%">
<div class=3D"c4"><a class=3D"c6" name=3D"syntaxe" id=3D"syntaxe">Syntax</a=
></div>
<p><b>Solresol</b> shortens phrases to make them logical, clear and easy to=
 understand for all peoples:</p>
<p>1=C2=BA Negation is indicated by a single word that is not repeated many=
 times unnecessarily. [This relates to a quirk of French grammar irrelevant=
 to English speakers (except those who use double negatives). I have left t=
he French originals to furnish example sentences.]</p>
<div class=3D"c4">EXAMPLES:</div>
<blockquote><i>Je</i> <b>ne</b> <i>veux</i> <b>pas</b> <i>partir,</i> <b>Dr=
 d fsf fsor</b>. <i>I don't want to leave.</i><br>
<i>Nous</i> <b>n</b>'<i>allons</i> <b>jamais</b> <i>l=C3=A0,</i> <b>Dr' frf=
 ls lm</b>. <i>We never go there.</i><br>
<i>Tu</i> <b>ne</b> <i>comprends</i> <b>pas</b> <i>leur lettre,</i> <b>Dm d=
 flf rs fdm</b>. <i>You don't understand their letter.</i><br></blockquote>
<p>2=C2=BA One must be wary of phrases or constructions where one finds idi=
oms and metaphors with figurative meanings; these phrases will not be under=
stood by foreigners.<br>
<b>Solresol</b> must restore the proper, true, simple, clear meaning with p=
recise words.</p>
<div class=3D"c4">EXAMPLES:</div>
<p>Do not say: <i>get the drift [of],</i> but: <i>understand</i>, <b>flf</b=
>.<br>
Do not say: <i>how are you doing?</i> but: <i>Are you well?</i> <b>rdff?</b=
><br>
Do not say: <i>pass away,</i> say: <i>die</i>, <b>rfmd</b>.<br>
Do not say: <i>have every hair in place</i>, say: <i>be correct</i>, <b>frm=
 srso</b>.<br>
On ne dira pas: <i>feel hollow,</i> say: <i>be hungry</i>, <b>dsod</b>.</p>
<p>3=C2=BA One always places the adjective after the substantive.<br>
So one never says: joyful baby, unhappy friend, honest citizen, good food; =
but:</p>
<p><i>Baby joyful,</i> <b>dmfso sosr.</b><br>
<i>Friend unhappy,</i> <b>mds sosm</b>.<br>
<i>Citizen honest,</i> <b>sdrd dfsso</b>.<br>
<i>Food good,</i> <b>dlfr fl.</b><br></p>
<hr class=3D"c5" width=3D"20%" noshade=3D"">
<div class=3D"c15"><a name=3D"fasi" id=3D"fasi">Fasi Sifa</a></div>
<p><b>Solresol</b> uses these two words to indicate four modifications of t=
he same idea.</p>
<p>1=C2=BA <b>Fs</b> (<i>much, very</i>) placed before an adjective is <i>a=
ugmentative</i>.<br>
Example: <b>fl</b>, <i>good</i>; <b>fs fl</b>, <i>very good.</i></p>
<p>2=C2=BA <b>Fs</b> placed after an adjective is the <i>superlative</i>.<b=
r>
Example: <b>fl fs</b>, <i>extremely good, the most delicious.</i></p>
<p>3=C2=BA <b>Sf</b> (<i>little, slight</i>), placed before an adjective is=
 the <i>diminutive</i>.<br>
Example: <b>Sf fl</b>, <i>somewhat good.</i></p>
<p>4=C2=BA <b>Sf</b> placed after an adjective is <i>double diminutive</i>.=
<br>
Example: <b>fl sf</b>, <i>not very good, almost bad.</i></p>
<p>It is the same for substantives.</p>
<table>
<caption>EXAMPLES:</caption>
<tbody><tr>
<td><b>Ssr</b>,</td>
<td class=3D"c12">wind</td>
<td><b>Sf ssr</b>,</td>
<td class=3D"c12">slight wind, breeze</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><b>Fs ssr</b>,</td>
<td class=3D"c12">gale</td>
<td><b>Ssr sf</b>,</td>
<td class=3D"c12">faint breeze, gentle breeze</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"c13">Ssr fs,</td>
<td class=3D"c12">very strong wind, violent tempest,</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td></td>
<td class=3D"c12">violent hurricane, cyclone</td>
</tr>
</tbody></table>
<hr class=3D"c5" width=3D"20%">
<div class=3D"c4"><a class=3D"c6" name=3D"partitif" id=3D"partitif">Partiti=
ve</a></div>
<p>To express a certain indeterminate amount, a vague quantity, <b>Solresol=
</b> omits the partitive or indefinite words, as well as the article in the=
 singular.</p>
<div class=3D"c4">EXAMPLES:</div>
<p><i>I would like</i> <b>some</b> <i>beer and</i> <b>a</b> <i>pastry,</i> =
becomes: <i>I would like beer and pastry,</i> <b>dr mfl dsfr r dsrs</b>.<br=
>
<i>Give [me] a meter</i> <b>of</b> <i>muslin</i>, becomes: <i>Give [me] met=
er muslin,</i> <b>rml rdd lsorf ldld</b>.<br>
<i>The enemy has a very large number of troops,</i> becomes: <i>enemy has t=
roops much</i> (in the superlative), <b>Sdm fmso fmfr fs</b>.</p>
<p>To sum up, <b>Solresol</b> makes expression of thought concise and gives=
 a brief, clear, true and precise translation that is perfectly accessible =
to all nations.</p>
<hr class=3D"c5" width=3D"40%">
<div class=3D"c4"><a class=3D"c6" name=3D"ecrit" id=3D"ecrit">Different kin=
ds of writing</a></div>
<p>In <b>Solresol</b> one can write in many ways:</p>
<p>1=C2=BA In all letters: <b>do, re, mi, fa, sol, la, si</b>.</p>
<p>2=C2=BA Omitting the vowels (except the <b>o</b> of <b>sol</b> to distin=
guish it from <b>si</b>): <b>d, r, m, f, so, l, s.</b></p>
<p>3=C2=BA In notes on a musical scale of just three lines, without knowing=
 music;</p>
<p><img src=3D"https://mozai.com/writing/not_mine/solresol/portee.gif" alt=
=3D"-"></p>
<p>4=C2=BA With the first 7 numbers, representing the seven notes, the numb=
ers being known in all countries.</p>
